STAR detectors have large acceptance of two pi azimuthal angle. The experiment at STAR [1] mainly focuses on event by event correlations and fluctuations, particle identification and jet like correlations. The main detector Time Projection Chamber (TPC) covers the mid-rapidity, \(|\eta|<1.3\). In the forward rapidity, \(2.5<|\eta|<4\), there are Forward Time Projection Chambers. We will introduce the detectors at STAR in detail later.

PHENIX detectors have relatively smaller acceptance but are detectors with fast data taking. The experiment at PHENIX [1] mainly focuses on heavy flavor, copiously produced hadron identification (pion, kaon and proton) and lepton identification. A spectrometer with two arms and systems of tracking, which is used to record the infor

