### 5.3 System and Centrality Dependence of \(v_{2}\)

The centrality and system-size dependence of \(v_{2}\) is related to the physics of the system created in high energy nuclear collisions. In the ideal hydrodynamic limit the centrality dependence of elliptic flow is mostly defined by the elliptic anisotropy of the overlapping region of the colliding nuclei, and in the low-density limit by the product of the elliptic anisotropy and the multiplicity. Thus, the centrality and system-size dependence of elliptic flow should be a good indicator of the degree of equilibration reached in the reaction [Vol00a].

